===Etymology===
From {{etyl|frm|en}} {{term|cariatide|lang=frm}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|caryatides|lang=la}}, from {{etyl|grc|en}} {{term|Καρυάτιδες||lang=grc}}, plural of {{term| Καρυᾶτις||lang=grc|a priestess of Artemis, female figures used as bearing-shafts}}, from {{term|Καρυατίζω||lang=grc|dance the Karyatid festival dance}} from {{term|Καρύαι||a town in Laconia with a temple of Artemis and a festival|lang=grc}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A sculpted female figure serving as an [[architectural]] element, used as a support for [[entablature]].

